W: 1. If I had another penny,
W: I would have another gill;
W: I would make the piper play
W: "The Bonny Lads o’ Byker Hill."
W:
W: Chorus:
W: Byker Hill and Walker Shore,
W: Collier lads for evermore!
W: Byker Hill and Walker Shore,
W: Collier lads for evermore!
W:
W: 2. The pitman and the keelman trim,
W: They drink bumble made from gin.
W: Then to dance they do begin
W: To the tune of Elsie Marley.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 3. When first I went down to the dirt
W: I had no cowl nor no pitshirt.
W: Now I’ve gotten two or three,
W: Walker Pit’s done well by me.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 4. Geordie Charlton, he had a pig,
W: He hit it with a shovel and it danced a jig,
W: All the way to Walker Shore
W: To the tune of Elsie Marley.
W: (Chorus)
